{"headword":"שָׂחַק","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>vb.</strong> laugh <strong>(</strong>‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">צהק</span>, q.v.; NH <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂחַק</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">סָחַק</span>; Ethiopic ሠሐቀ: <strong>)</strong>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">וְשׂ׳</span> consec. <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 29:9\" href=\"/Proverbs.29.9\">Pr 29:9</a>; 3 pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">שָֽׂחֲקוּ</span> <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 1:7\" href=\"/Lamentations.1.7\">La 1:7</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 30:1\" href=\"/Job.30.1\">Jb 30:1</a>; Impf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">יִשְׂחַק</span> <a data-ref=\"Job 39:7\" href=\"/Job.39.7\">Jb 39:7</a> +, etc.; Inf. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">שְׂחוֹק</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:27\" href=\"/Judges.16.27\">Ju 16:27</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 3:4\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.3.4\">Ec 3:4</a>;—"},{"senses":[{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>laugh</em> at, usually in contempt, derision, c. <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל</span> pers. <a data-ref=\"Job 30:1\" href=\"/Job.30.1\">Jb 30:1</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 52:8\" href=\"/Psalms.52.8\">ψ 52:8</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">עַל</span> rei <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 1:7\" href=\"/Lamentations.1.7\">La 1:7</a>; c. ל pers. God subj. <a data-ref=\"Psalms 37:13\" href=\"/Psalms.37.13\">ψ 37:13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Psalms 59:9\" href=\"/Psalms.59.9\">59:9</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">לָעַג</span>); c. ל rei vel pers. = have no fear of, <a data-ref=\"Habakkuk 1:10\" href=\"/Habakkuk.1.10\">Hb 1:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 5:22\" href=\"/Job.5.22\">Jb 5:22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 31:25\" href=\"/Proverbs.31.25\">Pr 31:25</a>, also, fig., of noble animals <a data-ref=\"Job 39:7\" href=\"/Job.39.7\">Jb 39:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Job 39:18\" href=\"/Job.39.18\">18</a>, <a data-ref=\"Job 39:22\" href=\"/Job.39.22\">22</a>; <a data-ref=\"Job 41:21\" href=\"/Job.41.21\">41:21</a>; abs., <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 29:9\" href=\"/Proverbs.29.9\">Pr 29:9</a> (opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">רָגַז</span>), of <span dir=\"rtl\">י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 2:4\" href=\"/Psalms.2.4\">ψ 2:4</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">לָעַג</span>), of wisdom <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 1:26\" href=\"/Proverbs.1.26\">Pr 1:26</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ב</span> temp.; ‖ id.)."}],"num":"a."},{"senses":[{"definition":"c. <span dir=\"rtl\">אֶל</span> pers., appar. of friendly laugh <a data-ref=\"Job 29:24\" href=\"/Job.29.24\">Jb 29:24</a>; in gen. <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 3:4\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.3.4\">Ec 3:4</a> (opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">בָּכָה</span>)."}],"num":"b."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>sport, play</em>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:27\" href=\"/Judges.16.27\">Ju 16:27</a>."}],"num":"2."}],"form":"Qal"},{"senses":[{"definition":"Pf. 1 s. <span dir=\"rtl\">וְשִׂחַקְתִּ֫י</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 6:21\" href=\"/I_Samuel.6.21\">1 S 6:21</a>; Impf. 3 ms. <span dir=\"rtl\">וַיְשַׂחֶק־</span> <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:25\" href=\"/Judges.16.25\">Ju 16:25</a>, etc.; Inf. cstr. <span dir=\"rtl\">לְשַׂחֶק־</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 104:26\" href=\"/Psalms.104.26\">ψ 104:26</a>; Pt. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְשַׂחֵק</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 26:19\" href=\"/Proverbs.26.19\">Pr 26:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 15:29\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.15.29\">1 Ch 15:29</a>, f. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְשַׂחֶ֫קֶת</span> <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 8:30\" href=\"/Proverbs.8.30\">Pr 8:30</a>, <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 8:31\" href=\"/Proverbs.8.31\">31</a>; pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְשַׂחֲקִים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 6:5\" href=\"/II_Samuel.6.5\">2 S 6:5</a> +, <span dir=\"rtl\">מְשַׂחֲקוֹת</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 18:7\" href=\"/I_Samuel.18.7\">1 S 18:7</a>;—"},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>make sport</em>, <a data-ref=\"Judges 16:25\" href=\"/Judges.16.25\">Ju 16:25</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ל</span> pers.) <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 2:14\" href=\"/II_Samuel.2.14\">2 S 2:14</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">לִפְנֵי</span> pers.; in tournament), <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 8:30\" href=\"/Proverbs.8.30\">Pr 8:30</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(לִפְנֵי)</span>, v <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 8:31\" href=\"/Proverbs.8.31\">31</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ב</span> loc.)."}],"num":"1."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>jest</em>, <a data-ref=\"Proverbs 26:19\" href=\"/Proverbs.26.19\">Pr 26:19</a>."}],"num":"2."},{"senses":[{"definition":"<em>play:</em> incl. instr. music, singing and dancing <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 18:7\" href=\"/I_Samuel.18.7\">1 S 18:7</a>, c. <span dir=\"rtl\">לִפְנֵי י׳</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 6:5\" href=\"/II_Samuel.6.5\">2 S 6:5</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">ב</span> instr.), = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 13:8\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.13.8\">1 Ch 13:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 6:21\" href=\"/II_Samuel.6.21\">2 S 6:21</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 15:29\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.15.29\">1 Ch 15:29</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">מְרַקֵּד</span>); of merry-making <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 15:17\" href=\"/Jeremiah.15.17\">Je 15:17</a> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">עָלַז</span>), <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 30:19\" href=\"/Jeremiah.30.19\">30:19</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 31:4\" href=\"/Jeremiah.31.4\">31:4</a>; of children’s sport <a data-ref=\"Zechariah 8:5\" href=\"/Zechariah.8.5\">Zc 8:5</a>; of beasts <a data-ref=\"Job 40:20\" href=\"/Job.40.20\">Jb 40:20</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 104:26\" href=\"/Psalms.104.26\">ψ 104:26</a>; of man, <em>play</em> with <span dir=\"rtl\">(ב)</span> crocod. <a data-ref=\"Job 40:29\" href=\"/Job.40.29\">Jb 40:29</a>."}],"num":"3."}],"form":"Pi."},{"senses":[{"definition":"(declar.) Pt. pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">מַשְׂחִיקִים</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 30:10\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.30.10\">2 Ch 30:10</a> they <em>uttered mockery</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">עֲלֵיהֶם</span> (‖ <span dir=\"rtl\">מַלְעִגִים</span>)."}],"form":"Hiph."}]},"rid":"BDB09655","strong_numbers":["7832"],"next_hw":"שְׂחֹק","prev_hw":"שָׂחִיף","all_cited":true,"root":true,"quotes":[],"GK":["8471"],"TWOT":["1905c"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}